Reason:
The bug occurs because the code does not differentiate between an existing `tcegrp` that is found in the loop and a newly allocated `tcegrp`. If an error occurs after allocating memory for `tcegrp`, the error handling incorrectly attempts to free it even if it was not newly allocated, leading to potential double-free or use-after-free issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
goto free_exit;
...
if (ret && tcegrp)
    kfree(tcegrp);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a new error handling case by using `goto free_exit` instead of `goto unlock_exit` when an error occurs after the allocation. This ensures that the memory is only freed if an error occurs and `tcegrp` was successfully allocated, preventing incorrect memory deallocation for already existing groups.

